            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Persian for a risk, then the Persian for to take a risk."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: بسته به",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "بسته به (baste be) — \"depending on\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "قیمت بسته به فصل فرق میکند. qeymat baste be fasl farq mikonad. The price varies depending on the season."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Baste \"bound\" + be \"to\". It takes a noun or a clause: baste be inke …."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "بسته به (baste be) is native Persian, literally \"bound to\": baste is the participle of bastan \"to bind\", which EtymDB traces to PIE bʰendʰ- \"to bind\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for telling, explaining and describing at B1."
