          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "به محض اینکه (be mahz-e inke) — \"as soon as\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "به محض اینکه رسیدم، به تو زنگ میزنم. be mahz-e inke residam, be to zang mizanam. As soon as I arrive, I will call you."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "It takes the past even for a future event: be mahz-e inke residam — as soon as I arrive."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "به محض اینکه (be mahz-e inke) is literally \"at the mere fact that\": mahz is usually traced to Arabic maḥḍ \"pure, mere\", and be and inke \"that\" are Persian."
            }
          ]
        },
