          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "تا زمانی که (tâ zamâni ke) — \"as long as; until\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "تا زمانی که اینجا هستی، میتوانی از اتاق من استفاده کنی. tâ zamâni ke injâ hasti, mitavâni az otâq-e man estefâde koni. As long as you are here, you can use my room."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "With a negative verb it means \"until\": tâ zamâni ke nayâyad — until he comes."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "تا زمانی که (tâ zamâni ke) is literally \"until the time that\": tâ is inherited Persian (EtymDB traces it to Middle Persian \"until, so that\"), and zamân comes from Arabic zamān \"time\"."
            }
          ]
        },
